From f549e27ab374e34fcf97c5344ed701d53c12cc0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:32:28 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 06/29] sceFontGetFontInfo: report the glyphs' bits per pixel

SceFontInfo ends with the font style and then the bits per pixel of the
glyph bitmaps (byte 260), which was left as the game had it, zero. A game
that sizes its glyph buffers from it computed a line length of zero,
allocated empty buffers 48 bytes apart and asked for every glyph with a
line length of zero, so each string was drawn over the next and all text
came out as stripes. It is now 4.

Verified on Windows with <prefix>_TRACE_FONT (bytes per line 48 for a
96-pixel 4-bit buffer, was 0) and captures of a menu before and after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 host/hle/hle_font.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/host/hle/hle_font.cpp b/host/hle/hle_font.cpp
index 5ff3cdc..4758110 100644
--- a/host/hle/hle_font.cpp
+++ b/host/hle/hle_font.cpp
@@ -113,6 +113,12 @@ void write_font_info(psprecomp::GuestMemory &memory, std::uint32_t address) {
     memory.store16(address + 82u, static_cast<std::uint16_t>(fonts::kCell));  // max glyph bitmap height
     memory.store32(address + 84u, 0x10000u);                                  // glyph count
     memory.store32(address + 88u, 0u);                                        // shadow map length
+    // The font's style (168 bytes from +92) is left as the game had it; then
+    // the bits per pixel of the glyph bitmaps, which the glyphs are drawn at
+    // whatever format the game asks for. A game may size its glyph buffers
+    // from it: left at zero, one computed a line length of zero, allocated
+    // empty buffers and laid every string over the next.
+    memory.store8(address + 260u, 4u);
 }
 
 // A game may keep every glyph it has drawn in a texture atlas and draw it
